      "rationale": "Whether a source_id was linked reflects data completeness/traceability at intake, plausibly associated with approval vs decline, and is knowable prior to the outcome."
    },
    {
      "name": "processed_date_present",
      "role": "leakage",
      "is_predictor": false,
      "rationale": "Presence of a processed_date is populated as part of processing/adjudication. It is only knowable after the outcome and is likely deterministically tied to whether/how the expense was resolved, constituting outcome leakage."
    },
    {
      "name": "ci_specificity",
      "role": "predictor",
      "is_predictor": true,
      "rationale": "Granularity of the configuration item reference (named model vs generic label) reflects documentation quality at submission and can plausibly predict decline; external to the outcome."
    },
    {
      "name": "vendor_brand",
      "role": "predictor",
      "is_predictor": true,
      "rationale": "Vendor/brand of the purchase is known at intake and can plausibly correlate with decline rates (approved vendors vs others); a legitimate predictor, not a restatement of the focus."
    }
  ],
  "n_predictors": 5,
  "predictive_utility": 0.55,
  "rationale": "Five of six columns are legitimate, pre-outcome features engineered from item, source, documentation, and vendor metadata that plausibly carry signal about decline likelihood, adding leverage beyond the raw columns. processed_date_present is a leakage feature: a processed date is typically populated during/after adjudication, so it is not knowable before the outcome and likely encodes the outcome itself. As a set the added columns provide moderate genuine predictive value, but the presence of a leaky column and the correlational (not strongly causal) nature of the rest caps the utility."
}
